course: dictionary
lesson: 1378
title: The capercaillie and clues in context
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Sometimes a word is new, but the sentence around it gives you clues. «The capercaillie, hlukhar or "the deaf one" in Ukrainian, is the biggest grouse.» The word biggest tells you a capercaillie is a large bird, and grouse tells you it belongs to a family of birds.
explain: Read on for more clues. «For a moment in its clicking spring song it seems not to hear, and it is now rare.» Clicking and song are sounds, so the capercaillie is making a noise in spring. Rare tells you there are not many left.
explain: Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then try your guess in the sentence. If "a large wild bird" fits where "capercaillie" is, your guess is right.
fact: A capercaillie is a very large wild bird of the grouse family.
fact: Capercaillies live in pine forests in Scotland, Scandinavia and other cold parts of Europe and Asia.
fact: In spring, the males are black and puff out their tails, and they make clicking and popping sounds to attract females.
fact: «Hlukhar» is the Ukrainian name for the capercaillie, and it means "the deaf one".
fact: In Scotland the capercaillie is endangered, so people work hard to protect it.
exercise: What is a capercaillie? | A small songbird that sings in gardens | A kind of pine tree | A type of fish that lives in rivers | *A very large wild bird of the grouse family
exercise: «The capercaillie is the biggest grouse.» Which word tells you the bird is large? | *biggest | capercaillie | grouse | is
exercise: Where do capercaillies live? | In hot deserts with sand dunes | At the bottom of the sea | *In cold pine forests in Scotland and Scandinavia
test: In spring, why do male capercaillies make clicking and popping sounds? | To warn people to go away | *To attract females | To ask for food | To cool down in the sun
test: «Hlukhar» means "the deaf one" in Ukrainian. What is the capercaillie's name in Ukrainian? | Carpathians | Polissia | *Hlukhar | Lynx
exam: Which clue in «turkey-sized capercaillies» tells you the bird is big? | *turkey-sized | capercaillies | black | forests
